Repository Update Log: May 22, 2026
Overview
Successfully transitioned the local automation framework from a passive telemetry log into a functional, bi-directional local communication pipeline. This iteration standardizes local script integration, establishes an architectural pattern for recursive data tracking, and verifies automated cloud redundancy.

Key Implementations & Engineering Milestones
Pipeline Exception Handling: Resolved parameter and syntax blockers within the primary data capture loop (listener.ps1), enabling stable, continuous terminal execution.

Bi-Directional Communication Layer: Updated the core orchestration module (orchestrator.ps1) to process input streams, compute an 8-bit binary string array for the transactional ledger, and emit real-time system execution acknowledgments.

Telemetry Logging Framework: Introduced a structured database schema (learning.db) that captures, timestamps, and appends real-time script activity to provide data blocks for future recursive refinement engines.

Hardened Redundancy Replication: Standardized mirroring parameters utilizing local robocopy mechanisms to map active system workspaces into dual cloud-synchronized target directories (AI_Dispatch and AI_Vault).
